I found the concrete cause: Lean asks `/proc/<namespace-pid>/exe`, but this audit container’s `/proc` mount exposes a different PID namespace, so that path is absent. This explains both Lean’s “failed to locate application” and Lake’s configuration failure. I’m applying a narrow temporary compatibility shim under `/tmp/audit-work` that only redirects that failed self-executable lookup to `/proc/self/exe`, then rerunning the trusted checker unchanged.
